sequenceDiagram
    participant App as App<br>[implements GapCentralResponse]
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GapCentral]

    Note over App, Node: Precondition: connected,<br>IoCapabilities set for passkey entry<br>(display and/or keyboard).

    App->>Node: GapCentral.PairAndBond()

    alt Node displays passkey, user enters it on peer
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.AuthenticationRequired(<br>isNumericComparison=false, passkey=485923)
        Note over App: Display 485923. User reads it and types it on the peer device.<br>No AuthenticateWithPasskey call is required on our side.

        alt Peer accepts the correct passkey
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)
        else Peer enters wrong passkey
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(<br>pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=passkeyEntryFailed)
        end
    else Peer displays passkey, user enters it on us
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.AuthenticationRequired(<br>isNumericComparison=false)
        Note over App: passkey field is unused in this variant.<br>User reads the passkey shown on the peer and types it into the App UI.

        App->>Node: GapCentral.AuthenticateWithPasskey(485923)

        alt Correct passkey
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)
        else Wrong passkey
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(<br>pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=passkeyEntryFailed)
        end
    end

    Note over App, Node: In both variants, no response within the 30 s SMP timeout results in<br>PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=timeout).
